<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Skin</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Ranger (guild level 2), Druid (guild level 12, up to 80%)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>skin corpse
</pre>
<p>Takes the hide, fur or scales from a corpse. Sell it for money, or keep 
it as a trophy. You need a dagger to do it, carried or wielded, and it 
costs endurance, more for a big beast. You must be standing.
</p><p>Your skill and dexterity decide how well it goes, against the creature's 
level: the mightier the beast, the harder its skin is to take cleanly. A 
fine skin from a rare creature is worth a good deal; a botched one, 
mangled by your knife, is worth nothing. Either way, a corpse can only be 
skinned once. Some creatures have no skin worth taking.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
